<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=sword">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Weapons and war</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sword</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 3300 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A sword is an edged weapon intended for manual cutting or thrusting, with a blade longer than that of a knife or dagger. The earliest weapons that can be called swords date to around 3300 BCE and come from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arslantepe">Arslantepe</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, where they were made of arsenical bronze and were about 60 cm long. Blades longer than that were impractical until the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a>, because bronze is not stiff, and the first unambiguous swords are Minoan examples from about 1700 BCE of more than 100 cm. Iron swords became common from the 13th century BCE, and the later spatha, rapier, sabre and katana developed from the same weapon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sword.jpg" alt="Sword" width="330" height="71" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Søren Niedziella from Denmark · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albion_Hospitaller_Medieval_Sword_1_(6092737619)_(II).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 3300 BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Arslantepe, Turkey</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>Minoan Crete (c. 1700 BCE); Indus Valley (1700-1400 BCE)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>One dating gives about 1600 BCE for the earliest specimens, while another dates the first weapons that can be called swords to about 3300 BCE at Arslantepe; the first swords beyond ambiguity are Minoan, from about 1700 BCE.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/copper-smelting">Copper smelting<span>c. 5000 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/bronze">Bronze<span>c. 4650 BCE</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=sword">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
